rophic defeat after another and were driven back in disarray. Finally, at the gates of Moscow, the Red Army managed to turn the tables and what followed was the bloodiest conflict in history which ended with the unconditional surrender of Nazi Germany. During the conflict Soviet Union alone suffered 26,6 millions dead, 14,6 million civilians and 12 millions soldiers, which was 14% of the Soviet pre-war population. The  economic damages were also huge, between 1940-1945 the Soviet GDP fell by 20% and what followed was years of drought, famine and typhus epidemics. It is a fact that the sacrifices of the people of Soviet Union were by far the greatest of the Allied nations.","LocalizedString":"At the start of Operation Barbarossa the Soviet Union faced the largest invasion in history. In the first five months of the invasion the Red Army suffered one catastrophic defeat after another and were driven back in disarray. Finally, at the gates of Moscow, the Red Army managed to turn the tables and what followed was the bloodiest conflict in history which ended with the unconditional surrender of Nazi Germany. During the conflict Soviet Union alone suffered 26,6 millions dead, 14,6 million civilians and 12 millions soldiers, which was 14% of the Soviet pre-war population. The  economic damages were also huge, between 1940-1945 the Soviet GDP fell by 20% and what followed was years of drought, famine and typhus epidemics. It is a fact that the sacrifices of the people of Soviet Union were by far the greatest of the Allied nations."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Breakthrough","isReserved":true,"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Mother_Russia'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/OrdersFeb17/Mother_Russia.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Soviet/03_Breakthrough/T_at_all_cost.T_at_all_cost","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Alamy Stock Photos","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/G